# Build context. Everything not needed to BUILD is excluded, which keeps the
# context small and — more importantly — keeps host state out of the image.
# A node_modules built on Windows contains platform-specific binaries that
# would silently override the Linux ones installed inside the container.

**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
.githooks

# Never. Production credentials live in the environment's secret store
# (INFRASTRUCTURE §6), and a .env copied into an image is a secret baked into
# every layer that follows it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

ui-prototype
docs
database/tests
tests
tools/parity

**/*.md
!README.md
